   "source": [
    "# 04 — Missing Data in Time Series: Beyond Simple Imputation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Companion notebook to Article 4 of the *Time Series Feature Engineering* series.**\n",
    "\n",
    "📖 Read the article: [Medium](https://medium.com/@asidd24/missing-data-in-time-series-beyond-simple-imputation-edae6e2543c7) · [LinkedIn Newsletter](https://www.linkedin.com/newsletters/time-series-engineered-7485187061080137728/)\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Missing Data Mechanisms in Time Series**: MCAR vs MAR vs MNAR.\n",
    "2. **Baseline Imputation Failures**: Why mean imputation and backward-fill create catastrophic leakage.\n",
    "3. **Seasonal-Aware Imputation**: Preserving weekly/daily cycles across missing gaps (`seasonal_fill`).\n",
    "4. **STL-Based Reconstruction**: Rebuilding trend + seasonality over extended multi-week gaps (`stl_imputation`).\n",
    "5. **Missingness as a Feature**: Engineering explicit indicator columns (`was_missing`, `days_since_observed`, `run_of_missing`).\n",
    "6. **Production Imputation Pipeline**: Putting it all together into a robust production-grade pipeline (`robust_time_series_imputation`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b57813a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c5d6846b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.append('..')  # Allow importing from src/\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.data import generate_daily_sales\n",
    "from src.features import (\n",
    "    seasonal_fill,\n",
    "    stl_imputation,\n",
    "    add_missingness_features,\n",
    "    robust_time_series_imputation\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_style('whitegrid')\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (12, 4)\n",
    "plt.rcParams['axes.grid'] = True\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7dffce75",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Generating Time Series Data with Missing Gaps\n",
    "\n",
    "We generate 2 years of daily sales data with weekly seasonality and trend, and inject three types of missingness patterns:\n",
    "- **Short random gaps** (MCAR - Missing Completely at Random)\n",
    "- **Systematic weekend gaps** (MAR - Missing at Random)\n",
    "- **Extended multi-week outage gap** (e.g. 21-day sensor/IT failure)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3243f6b2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Generate clean 2-year daily sales series\n",
    "clean_sales = generate_daily_sales(n_days=730, seed=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create series with missing data\n",
    "sales_missing = clean_sales.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Short MCAR gaps (random single-day missing values)\n",
    "mcar_idx = np.random.choice(len(sales_missing), size=30, replace=False)\n",
    "sales_missing.iloc[mcar_idx] = np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Extended gap (21 consecutive days outage in month 6)\n",
    "sales_missing.iloc[180:201] = np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Total observations: {len(clean_sales)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Missing observations: {sales_missing.isna().sum()} ({sales_missing.isna().mean():.1%})\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "plot_gaps",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "ax.plot(clean_sales.index, clean_sales.values, label='True Signal (Clean)', alpha=0.5, color='gray')\n",
    "ax.plot(sales_missing.index, sales_missing.values, label='Observed Signal (with Missing Gaps)', color='tab:blue', linewidth=1.5)\n",
    "ax.axvspan(sales_missing.index[180], sales_missing.index[200], color='tab:red', alpha=0.2, label='21-Day Extended Outage')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Time Series with Injected Missing Data Gaps')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Sales')\n",
    "ax.legend(loc='upper left')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "baseline_imputation",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. The Pitfalls of Baseline Imputation Techniques\n",
    "\n",
    "Common tabular imputation techniques destroy time series dynamics:\n",
    "- **Mean Imputation**: Flattens variation, distorts standard deviation, introduces artificial jumps.\n",
    "- **Backward-Fill (`bfill`)**: **FUTURE LEAKAGE!** Uses future unobserved values at time $t$.\n",
    "- **Linear Interpolation**: Works well for 1–2 missing points, but flattens seasonal peaks over multi-day gaps."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "compare_baselines",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Slice window around the 21-day gap\n",
    "slice_start, slice_end = 170, 210\n",
    "subset_clean = clean_sales.iloc[slice_start:slice_end]\n",
    "subset_missing = sales_missing.iloc[slice_start:slice_end]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply baseline methods\n",
    "ffill_series = subset_missing.ffill()\n",
    "linear_series = subset_missing.interpolate(method='linear')\n",
    "mean_series = subset_missing.fillna(subset_missing.mean())\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "ax.plot(subset_clean.index, subset_clean.values, 'k--', label='True Ground Truth', alpha=0.7)\n",
    "ax.plot(ffill_series.index, ffill_series.values, label='Forward Fill (ffill)', color='tab:orange')\n",
    "ax.plot(linear_series.index, linear_series.values, label='Linear Interpolation', color='tab:green')\n",
    "ax.plot(mean_series.index, mean_series.values, label='Mean Imputation', color='tab:purple', linestyle=':')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Baseline Imputation over a 21-Day Gap (Destroys Weekly Seasonality)')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Sales')\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "seasonal_stl",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Seasonal & STL-Based Imputation\n",
    "\n",
    "For periodic time series, we need methods that preserve trend and seasonal phase:\n",
    "1. `seasonal_fill`: Replaces missing values with observations from the exact same day of the week in prior cycles.\n",
    "2. `stl_imputation`: Uses STL decomposition to fit Trend + Seasonal components and reconstruct missing periods."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "apply_advanced",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Apply seasonal_fill and stl_imputation\n",
    "s_filled = seasonal_fill(sales_missing, period=7)\n",
    "stl_filled = stl_imputation(sales_missing, period=7)\n",
    "\n",
    "subset_s = s_filled.iloc[slice_start:slice_end]\n",
    "subset_stl = stl_filled.iloc[slice_start:slice_end]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "ax.plot(subset_clean.index, subset_clean.values, 'k--', label='True Ground Truth', alpha=0.8)\n",
    "ax.plot(subset_s.index, subset_s.values, label='Seasonal Fill (Lag-7 Phase Match)', color='tab:blue')\n",
    "ax.plot(subset_stl.index, subset_stl.values, label='STL Reconstruction (Trend + Seasonality)', color='tab:red', linewidth=2)\n",
    "ax.set_title('Advanced Imputation: Seasonal & STL Decomposition over 21-Day Gap')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Sales')\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "missingness_features",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Engineering Missingness Features\n",
    "\n",
    "Imputation is only half the story. Tree-based models (LightGBM, XGBoost) perform significantly better when we explicitly tell them **which values were imputed and how long the gap was**.\n",
    "\n",
    "We engineer three missingness features:\n",
    "- `was_missing`: Binary flag ($1$ if imputed, $0$ if original)\n",
    "- `days_since_observed`: Number of consecutive days since last valid observation\n",
    "- `run_of_missing`: Duration of current missing run"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "missingness_code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_missing = sales_missing.to_frame('sales')\n",
    "df_features = add_missingness_features(df_missing, 'sales')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Sample engineered missingness features during the outage:\")\n",
    "df_features.iloc[178:188]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "production_pipeline",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Robust Production Imputation Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "In production, a single rule doesn't fit all gap sizes:\n",
    "- **Short gaps ($\le 3$ days)**: Linear interpolation is fast and accurate.\n",
    "- **Long gaps ($> 3$ days)**: STL decomposition preserves trend + seasonality.\n",
    "- **Feature Matrix**: Automatically includes missingness indicators and gap lengths."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "robust_pipeline_code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "imputed_df = robust_time_series_imputation(sales_missing, period=7, gap_threshold=3)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Imputed dataset summary:\")\n",
    "print(imputed_df.head(10))\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTotal original missing: {imputed_df['was_missing'].sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Remaining missing values after pipeline: {imputed_df['value'].isna().sum()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "summary",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Key Takeaways\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Never use backward fill (`bfill`) or mean imputation** for time series targets — `bfill` causes future data leakage and mean imputation flattens variance.\n",
    "2. **Use Linear Interpolation for short gaps ($\le 3$ periods)** to maintain smoothness without heavy compute.\n",
    "3. **Use STL Decomposition for extended gaps ($> 3$ periods)** to reconstruct trend and seasonal cycles accurately.\n",
    "4. **Always pass missingness features (`was_missing`, `days_since_observed`) to tree models** so they can adjust uncertainty and prediction weights."
   ]
  }
 ],
